# Windows / React Native native-build requirement — read this before changing it.
#
# CMake mirrors every source file's ABSOLUTE path underneath the native build directory, so pnpm's store
# segment is duplicated into every object-file path. ninja.exe is not long-path aware (the
# LongPathsEnabled registry setting does not help it) and hard-fails at Windows' 260-character limit:
#   ninja: error: Stat(...ComponentDescriptors.cpp.o): Filename longer than 260 characters
#
# A hoisted layout resolves packages at node_modules/<pkg>/ instead of
# node_modules/.pnpm/<pkg>@<ver>_<32-char-hash>/node_modules/<pkg>/, removing ~40 characters from every
# mirrored path. That is the margin the build needs.
#
# Measured, not guessed: shortening the store instead (virtual-store-dir=C:/s plus
# virtual-store-dir-max-length=30) was tried first because it preserves pnpm's stricter isolated linker.
# It reclaimed real characters but still came out around 300 for react-native-safe-area-context's
# generated codegen path, which is ~85 characters on its own and cannot be shortened. Hoisting is the
# only option that fits.
#
# KNOWN HAZARD, mitigated: hoisting previously produced TWO copies of fastify (5.11.3 hoisted to the root
# and 5.12.1 under services/api). @fastify/cookie and @fastify/multipart sat at the root, so their
# `declare module "fastify"` augmentations attached to a different module identity than the one the API
# imports, and reply.setCookie / reply.clearCookie / request.file all vanished from the types — CI failed
# with ~10 TS2339 errors. The fix is the `pnpm.overrides.fastify` pin in the root package.json, which
# collapses it to a single copy. If a similar "property does not exist" error ever appears for another
# augmenting plugin, look for a duplicated peer first; do not assume the calling code is wrong.
node-linker=hoisted
